4. CpsFlowDefinition.java:120 - CpsFlowExecution creation with user-supplied script from @DataBoundConstructor (sandbox=true path bypasses ScriptApproval)
5. ReplayAction.java:214 - form.getString("mainScript") direct script injection entry point

Key findings: The sandbox flag is NOT user-controllable (correctly inherited from original execution), but the script CONTENT is fully user-controlled. Users with REPLAY permission (lower than admin) can inject arbitrary Groovy that executes in the CPS sandbox for sandboxed builds. Any sandbox escape achieves RCE on the Jenkins controller. Non-sandboxed builds require Jenkins.RUN_SCRIPTS (admin) permission, which is appropriately restrictive.
