2026-03-30 23:17:12 - Agent_20260330230751 - INFO - [+] Agent signaled completion: Reviewed 1 CodeQL finding (UUID: 20260330230649) for the Snippetizer HTTP endpoint `doGenerateSnippet` at line 487 in Snippetizer.java. The method accepts a user-controlled `json` query parameter that flows directly into `uberClassLoader.loadClass()` via `jsonO.getString("stapler-class")`, and then into `descriptor.newInstance(req, jsonO)`. There is no permission check (`@RequirePOST`, `checkPermission()`, or `hasPermission()`) in the method itself. The `@Restricted(DoNotUse.class)` annotation is a developer-facing compile-time warning only and does not restrict HTTP access. The generated Groovy snippet is returned as text and not executed server-side, so this is not a direct OS command injection (CWE-078) vulnerability. However, it requires manual review to determine if Jenkins' global security configuration adequately gates this endpoint, and whether any plugin descriptor's `newInstance()` could chain into OS command execution with attacker-controlled parameters. Submitted as manual review (mr) with medium severity.
